    <section xml:id='tests-IF-ELSE-IF-STATEMENT'>
      <title>Else-If Chains without a Final Else</title>
      <para>An if statement may chain an else if without a final else. Such a
        chain yields no value; when no condition holds, the statement falls
        through and any bindings keep their prior values. (Regression: the
        emitter used to merge the arms' values into a dead phi node that
        failed LLVM verification when the inner arm's value was computed
        inside its own branch.)</para>
