  <section xmlns='http://docbook.org/ns/docbook' xml:id='category-REPEAT-LOOPS'>
    <title>Repeat Loops</title>
    <para>A repeat loop runs its body forever and exits only through break (or
    return). Because break is the only way out, a break carrying a value
    (`break v`) makes the repeat an expression that yields that value.</para>

    <section xml:id='tests-REPEAT-BASIC'>
      <title>Repeat and Break Value</title>
      <para>The value of a repeat expression is the operand of the break
